 "overall": "B's correlated noise is REAL and is a per-pixel-scale sensor property: present in the dark (T2), fine-scale (T3), and stable to 1.35x across the eight unclipped pairs above the darkest group. But the pre-registered T1 criterion (<2x across all pairs) FAILED at 2.5x because the darkest group reads low, and the ACF sum rule implies a variance factor of 0.583, which OVERSHOOTS the observed 0.84 B/green ratio. So a pure mean-preserving filter is NOT the explanation, while a signal-proportional correlated component in B is established. Mechanism UNRULED -- outside M71's charter and not settleable from flat fields.",
